#title{A literate FizzBuzz}
#date{2026-11-07}
#tags{literate programming, go}

A bag that holds a code block is a named chunk, and a line holding only `<<<name>>>` links to it. That is
how the original barkdown labels code, and it turns a post into a small literate program. Follow the link in the first
block.

The program counts from 1 to 100.

#fizzbuzz{
  ```go
  func main() {
  	for i := 1; i <= 100; i++ {
  		<<<print one number>>>
  	}
  }
  ```
}

Multiples of 15 are tested first, because they are also multiples of 3 and of 5.

#print one number{
  ```go
  switch {
  case i%15 == 0:
  	fmt.Println("FizzBuzz")
  case i%3 == 0:
  	fmt.Println("Fizz")
  case i%5 == 0:
  	fmt.Println("Buzz")
  default:
  	fmt.Println(i)
  }
  ```
}
